WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.400
[tense music playing]

2
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.360
[exhales sharply]

3
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.960
[siren blaring]

4
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.680
[siren stops]

5
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.600
[man on radio] <i>Units maintain position.</i>
<i>No activity reported.</i>

6
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.960
[Mélanie] Okay. Yeah.

7
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.400
[man] Move over there.

8
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.480
[indistinct radio chatter]

9
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.080
[rifle safety clicks]

10
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.080
- Establish a perimeter around the vehicle.
- Copy.

11
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.880
[man on radio] <i>Maintain position.</i>
<i>No activity reported.</i>

12
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.440
[officers chattering indistinctly]

13
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.640
[Mélanie sighs]

14
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.160
Commander Berger. you know the procedure.

15
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.200
I'm placing you under arrest.

16
00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.080
Yeah.

17
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.880
ELITE FORCE

18
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.040
Sorry to have kept you waiting. Commander.
I'm sure this won't take long.

19
00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.280
[door slams]

20
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.120
[power-on beep]

21
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.680
I just have a… a few questions for you.
Clarifications.

22
00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.480
Now. you said your phone…
that you left it in your locker?

23
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.200
Yeah. that's right.
I forgot it in my locker.

24
00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.040
- Hm. It's not like you to be unreachable.
- My mind was elsewhere.

25
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.360
I don't make a habit
of revisiting painful memories.

26
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.640
I was pretty distraught. so… yeah.

27
00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.800
You went to visit the place
where your former partner was killed.

28
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.320
On the anniversary of his death. right?

29
00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:00.040
Have you ever gone to visit the place
in the 15 years since you… lost him?

30
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.160
Since he died?

31
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.640
No.

32
00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:03.880
Why this year?

33
00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.760
Maybe because of Christophe.

34
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.920
I just felt like I had to.

35
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.800
To pay your respects.

36
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.680
Yeah.

37
00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.480
Armed with an AK-47
and a pump-action shotgun.

38
00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.400
I'm a cautious kind of person.
You can understand that given my history.

39
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.120
I'm also quite a cautious person.

40
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.400
But it wouldn't cross my mind
to bring an arsenal with me

41
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.720
to visit my father's grave.

42
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.160
I think. possibly.
the difference between you and me

43
00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.040
is how dangerous
our respective professions are.

44
00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:36.280
Have you ever been targeted by a car bomb
in the course of your work?

45
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.040
You or your father?

46
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.360
Have you ever been. let's say.
maybe anxious. or terrified.

47
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.360
that because of what you do every day.
you might not make it home alive?

48
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.240
That you might not be able
to see your family?

49
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:52.400
And maybe if your job was.
I don't know. a bit more dangerous

50
00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.760
than simply handing out fines
to people doing their jobs.

51
00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.880
you might see things
a bit different. perhaps.

52
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.800
My father was a general
in the armed forces.

53
00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.280
Great point. though.

54
00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.320
I'm still struggling to understand
something about the weapons.

55
00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.680
- [David sighs]
- None of them were registered anywhere.

56
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.960
There are no permits for them.
They're not authorized for the field.

57
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.320
The weapons were seized
during a recent mission.

58
00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.640
I followed all the necessary steps
to have them regulated and made official.

59
00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.200
I imagine the papers
just got lost in the shuffle.

60
00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.440
So much bureaucratic red tape. you know.

61
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:26.840
Mea culpa.

62
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.440
I accept the fine.

63
00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.600
[scoffs]

64
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.160
Would you?

65
00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.480
SEALED - DO NOT OPEN

66
00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:45.880
90 rounds of ammo for the AK-47.
and 30 Brenneke shells for the shotgun.

67
00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.800
I'm confused. Commander.
I believe these aren't standard issue?

68
00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.720
We choose our ammunition
to suit the mission.

69
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.480
which you would know if you took
the slightest interest in our work.

70
00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.440
So? What kind of mission
would require this type of gear?

71
00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.360
One that demands overwhelming force.

72
00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.000
[scoffs]

73
00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.000
Just so I make sure
I understand correctly.

74
00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.960
you commandeered
an unregistered shotgun and rifle.

75
00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.160
with ammunition specially chosen
because of its firepower.

76
00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.760
You drove yourself to the site
of your former partner's death.

77
00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.880
illegally breaking
into a military site in the process.

78
00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.800
something you've never done before.
not once in 15 years.

79
00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.680
and there.
perhaps coincidentally. or by fate.

80
00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.280
you come across Mr. Mayard.

81
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.840
The sole suspect in the killing
of your commanding officer.

82
00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.440
You go to bring him in.

83
00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:41.160
and despite your. um… expertise
and your many years' experience at GIGN.

84
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.360
he grabs a weapon.
so you have to kill him. Is that right?

85
00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.440
Minus that hint of sarcasm. correct.

86
00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:54.000
I promised that if you
stepped out of line ever again.

87
00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.360
it would be the last time.

88
00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:59.560
I'm a woman of my word.
You're not coming back from this.

89
00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.280
[dramatic music playing]

90
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.520
[indistinct chatter]

91
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.200
[dramatic music continues]

92
00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:20.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

93
00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:23.840
[door opens]

94
00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.520
[woman] Now we both know. All right?

95
00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.600
[woman speaking indistinctly]

96
00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.400
[knocking]

97
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.880
[Mélanie] Yes?

98
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.960
[door opens]

99
00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.280
Mrs. Berger. come on in.

100
00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.680
[door closes]

101
00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.560
That's a police report.

102
00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.640
It was filed
by one of your daughter's friends.

103
00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.400
relating to events that took place
at his home. at a party.

104
00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:10.800
The young man describes
an altercation between David Berger

105
00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.600
and several of his guests.

106
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.040
If this were serious.

107
00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:17.400
the prosecutor on this case
would be laying charges on my husband.

108
00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.200
But this is just a police report.

109
00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.520
You're absolutely right.

110
00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.960
The young man in question
claimed he had too much to drink.

111
00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.680
and withdrew his statement.

112
00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.520
The prosecutor was therefore
unable to pursue the case.

113
00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.760
So. what? Why are you telling me this?

114
00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.880
Your husband
is formally trained in combat.

115
00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.600
He's more than capable in a fight.

116
00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.360
In short. he's a weapon.

117
00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.680
So when it's one o'clock in the morning.
his daughter's not answering her phone.

118
00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.720
maybe he panics.
And when he finds this guy…

119
00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.200
he tases him.

120
00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:53.280
The question I'm asking myself.
Mrs. Berger.

121
00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:56.880
is how far your husband's willing to go
when his family's on the line?

122
00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.400
[tense music playing]

123
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.200
[Jess exhales]

124
00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:05.720
David's calling is to protect.

125
00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.720
You. me. his daughter. everyone.

126
00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.400
The mission above all else. Always.

127
00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.880
He's just doing his job.

128
00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:24.040
And the premeditated murder of a suspect?

129
00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:26.720
That's just him doing his job as well?

130
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.800
How long have you been working
with Commander Berger?

131
00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.040
Five years.

132
00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.080
A bit longer.

133
00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.120
[tense music continues]

134
00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.120
[Mélanie] How would you
describe his leadership?

135
00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:43.960
Exemplary.

136
00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.320
Would you describe yourselves as close?
You and Berger?

137
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.240
We're all brothers-in-arms.
The GIGN is one big family.

138
00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:55.720
Hm.

139
00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.120
There's no sound in this video.

140
00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.280
but do you happen to recall
what you were saying to him here?

141
00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:05.280
Not really. no. probably nothing special.

142
00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:07.560
Something about our kids.
training. recruits.

143
00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:13.160
And this bag. it seems quite heavy.
Any idea what might be in it?

144
00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:14.280
[chuckles softly]

145
00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.960
It's from the armory. it's a tactical bag.
You know exactly what's in there.

146
00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.600
Why bother asking?

147
00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:23.880
[Mélanie] You didn't have
any shooting drills

148
00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.520
planned for that day. though. did you?

149
00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.760
Why take out weapons?

150
00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.560
Each one of us is an elite marksman.

151
00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:31.280
We spend plenty of time training.
That's not surprising.

152
00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.000
You seem a bit surprised in the video.

153
00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.440
If that's your interpretation.

154
00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.960
[sighs]

155
00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:44.120
I think you knew

156
00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.960
the commander wasn't using
that bag for training purposes.

157
00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.280
I think you tried to warn him.
because you're a good person.

158
00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:52.960
Loyal too.

159
00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.040
An admirable quality.

160
00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.520
But loyal to whom?
That's what you should be asking.

161
00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.840
Loyal to your men?

162
00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.600
Or to your friend?

163
00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.720
Do you think that driving out
to a decommissioned military base

164
00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.680
in the middle of the night.
stumbling upon a heavily armed suspect.

165
00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:13.600
and shooting him to death
is responsible behavior?

166
00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.240
Is that the behavior of a GIGN leader?

167
00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.280
The commander made a call.

168
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.200
Which was revenge. At the cost
of the entire institution's reputation.

169
00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.440
I won't even mention
the CL-20 that's disappeared

170
00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:31.200
that we have no hope of ever seeing again
now that our primary suspect is dead.

171
00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:32.400
What about you. Major?

172
00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.000
Who are you loyal to?

173
00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.320
[exhales]

174
00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.600
Tsk.

175
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.320
[sighs]

176
00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.080
[sighs]

177
00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.200
During the encounter with Kröller.

178
00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:00.120
when we were hit
by the sniper in the forest. uh…

179
00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.120
I can't be sure. but…

180
00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.280
I think he walked off with something.

181
00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.480
[Mélanie] Where were you last night?

182
00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.040
[tense music continues]

183
00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.080
I was at home. Alone in my apartment.

184
00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:25.880
[Mélanie] You weren't.

185
00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.200
You were there when he killed Mayard.

186
00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.640
You deliberately
concealed your presence there.

187
00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.080
Do you know what happens next?

188
00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:41.320
Your career is over.

189
00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:48.280
[door opens]

190
00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:52.040
[footsteps approach]

191
00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.520
[door closes]

192
00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:10.720
[ominous music playing]

193
00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:28.760
[Mélanie] You know what this is?

194
00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.800
Looks like a cartridge used by the sniper
who ambushed us in the forest

195
00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:47.920
and killed the arms dealer. Kröller.

196
00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.800
We found it in your home.

197
00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.400
Any idea why this might have been
in your apartment?

198
00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.840
As you know. long-range shooting
is one of my specialties. so…

199
00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.120
I've accumulated
a few cartridges over the years.

200
00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.480
Why do you think we went out of our way
to search your house?

201
00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.240
You're stubborn?

202
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:10.360
Major Bonenfant. your “brother-in-arms.”
your friend. your colleague. Cédric.

203
00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:13.280
He's the one who told me to look.

204
00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:16.080
You're aware that removing evidence
from a crime scene

205
00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.680
is in itself a crime
and would be grounds for a court martial?

206
00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.560
- But maybe it's a coincidence.
- [exhales]

207
00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.520
Like the weapons you took from the armory.

208
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:26.120
like the fact that you were
in the right place. at the right time.

209
00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.600
to take down the terrorist
everyone was looking for.

210
00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.240
But I have another explanation.

211
00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.240
Take a guess.

212
00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:33.560
Tsk. [sighs]

213
00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.960
Flashback to the night of the graduation.

214
00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.400
Your superior. your mentor.

215
00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.400
the man who taught you
everything you know.

216
00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.280
Christophe. is attacked.

217
00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.160
Your world falls apart.

218
00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.880
So you start your own investigation.

219
00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:50.880
You illegally interrogate a suspect
you just had arrested.

220
00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:53.560
You take away evidence from a crime scene.

221
00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.200
You track down Mayard.

222
00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.560
but he slips through your fingers
at the hospital.

223
00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:01.200
You keep searching.
You use your colleague's computer.

224
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:03.280
And then you find the guy.

225
00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.960
You go after him.

226
00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:09.240
And your investigation results
in personal. punitive justice.

227
00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.120
[door opens]

228
00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:15.000
Commander. a word. please?

229
00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:25.080
[slams door]

230
00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:29.360
Whenever a shot is fired. my men
are questioned. That's the procedure.

231
00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:32.320
I don't get involved
because it falls to the local police.

232
00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.160
Now I learn it's Internal Investigations

233
00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.160
that's been questioning my men
without telling me!

234
00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.280
Explain that.

235
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.360
I heard you brought in
David's wife for questioning.

236
00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:44.480
I just need to know
if this is you being overzealous.

237
00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.200
or if we've got a problem.

238
00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.080
Come in.

239
00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:53.120
[door opens]

240
00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:58.120
The SD card from your vehicle's dash cam
has mysteriously disappeared.

241
00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.080
Another coincidence.

242
00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.360
Fortunately. the dash cam's software
was updated.

243
00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.200
The footage gets uploaded to a server

244
00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.720
and I was able
to access the recording remotely.

245
00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:07.880
[general] Villiers?

246
00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:09.720
[tense music playing]

247
00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.760
- [general] David?
- [Mélanie] We all know you're guilty.

248
00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.960
The question now
is whether you'll get jail time.

249
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.160
When did you make the decision
to kill Mayard?

250
00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.640
And what role did your godson
play in your plan?

251
00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:49.120
Can you stop recording for a minute?

252
00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.840
And can he leave the room?

253
00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:53.520
[exhales]

254
00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:56.200
[footsteps receding]

255
00:14:57.800 --> 00:14:59.360
[door opens]

256
00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:00.960
[door closes]

257
00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:05.680
I'll confess to everything. The murder.
the weapons. the premeditation too.

258
00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.600
But on two conditions.

259
00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:12.040
The first is that Max
isn't dragged into this.

260
00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.680
He didn't know my plan
before following me.

261
00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:17.280
and I forced him
to keep quiet after the fact.

262
00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.280
The second…

263
00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.920
is that you let me
go home tonight. alright?

264
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.520
See my family.

265
00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:27.560
I'll provide a full confession tomorrow.

266
00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.800
You're still trying
to bend the rules to your advantage.

267
00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.240
even after getting caught.

268
00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:34.320
Why would I accept?

269
00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.920
Why wouldn't you accept
is a better question.

270
00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.560
For the moment. all you have

271
00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:44.480
is a lie about Max's involvement
in the whole situation.

272
00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:47.440
And a small series of minor infractions.

273
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:48.960
Not much to go on.

274
00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:52.360
We've got more than enough here
to discharge you and Max.

275
00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.920
- Yeah.
- Mm.

276
00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.320
But what would bring you
more satisfaction?

277
00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.200
Getting me kicked off the force?

278
00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.200
Or the chance to see me behind bars?

279
00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.880
- [dramatic music playing]
- [indistinct chatter]

280
00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.600
- Hey. you guys still awake?
- Hey. good. thanks.

281
00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:25.320
- Hey.
- All good?

282
00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.480
- All good.
- Hey.

283
00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:32.360
[instructor] Come on let's keep it up!

284
00:16:33.360 --> 00:16:34.640
[Cédric] Alright. move it!

285
00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.360
[man] Right. a little lower.
just a bit lower! And in on three!

286
00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:42.880
One. two. three! Let's go.

287
00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:44.560
- [instructor] Inside!
- [Cédric] Advance!

288
00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:48.280
[instructor] Good. breach the window!
Let's keep it moving. boys!

289
00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.360
[Cédric] You're taking too long.
Ten seconds and you're dead. got it?

290
00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:55.560
[instructor] Move up.
take a right. Right. now!

291
00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:58.240
[dramatic poignant music playing]

292
00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:03.400
[instructor] Go right!

293
00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:05.480
Advance!

294
00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:08.360
Hold here!

295
00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:16.200
[Cédric] Good work. debrief in ten.
Get changed and regroup at HQ.

296
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:19.000
[dramatic poignant music continues]

297
00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:24.240
We're with you. okay?

298
00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:27.120
You alright?

299
00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.560
Hey. asshole.

300
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:43.000
[dramatic poignant music continues]

301
00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.000
If you wanna talk. I'm around.

302
00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.320
It wouldn't change a thing.

303
00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.280
[dramatic poignant music continues]

304
00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:06.840
[exhales]

305
00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:20.680
[sighs]

306
00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.840
[motorcycle passes]

307
00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.600
[music fades]

308
00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:40.680
- [indistinct chatter]
- [sighs]

309
00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.880
Where were you?

310
00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:46.960
[door closes]

311
00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.920
I'm not here to talk.

312
00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:55.240
["My Chemical Soul"
by Laura Crow & Him playing]

313
00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.000
<i>♪ You should not believe</i>
<i>All that you see ♪</i>

314
00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:37.000
<i>♪ When they take control over me ♪</i>

315
00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.160
<i>♪ Forgive me if I'm cynical ♪</i>

316
00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.320
<i>♪ I'm driven by chemicals ♪</i>

317
00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:48.560
[playing "Impromptu No. 2"
by Franz Schubert]

318
00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:07.520
[footsteps approaching]

319
00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.000
[sighs]

320
00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:25.360
Since when does Internal
interrogate wives?

321
00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:27.880
She's overzealous. that's all.

322
00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.000
She thinks you executed
Christophe's killer.

323
00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.200
Why'd she let you go early?
They normally keep you for 24 hours.

324
00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:38.800
Because I confessed.

325
00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.200
You what?

326
00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.480
I made a deal with her.

327
00:20:42.560 --> 00:20:44.560
I'm signing anything she wants tomorrow.

328
00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:47.120
In exchange. she's letting me
spend the night with you.

329
00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.040
The night?

330
00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.200
What are you talking about?
Did you kill him or didn't you?

331
00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.120
I would've.

332
00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.040
[scoffs]

333
00:20:54.760 --> 00:20:56.720
What've you done? I can't believe this.

334
00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.840
You'll go to prison!

335
00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:02.160
[piano playing continues]

336
00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:05.680
It's because Max is involved. isn't it?
You don't owe him anything!

337
00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.120
[exhales. inhales sharply]

338
00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.600
What about Manon. David?

339
00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.800
You think I want to do this?
You think this is easy for me?

340
00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:21.760
I don't have a choice.

341
00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:22.840
It's Max.

342
00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:24.160
I have to help.

343
00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:27.760
It means nothing if you're here tonight
but can't be tomorrow.

344
00:21:31.120 --> 00:21:32.400
Nothing.

345
00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:51.120
[music ends]

346
00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:55.840
[Max sighs]

347
00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:03.080
Where are you going?

348
00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:05.280
It was fun. I gotta go.

349
00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:07.640
Hang on.

350
00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:11.440
You can't just go dark.
then show up at my door and say nothing.

351
00:22:12.320 --> 00:22:14.000
I told you. I wasn't here to talk.

352
00:22:14.080 --> 00:22:15.880
This is about David. right?

353
00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:18.640
Because he killed the terrorist?

354
00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.800
He cleaned out his locker.

355
00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:24.880
Apparently they fired him.

356
00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:27.120
[Max sighs]

357
00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:30.800
David didn't pull the trigger.

358
00:22:32.440 --> 00:22:33.600
I did.

359
00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:36.280
Wait. what?

360
00:22:36.360 --> 00:22:38.360
[dramatic music playing]

361
00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:41.480
Uh. what are you saying?

362
00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:45.040
I followed David. I was there.

363
00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.360
We stopped the guy together.
but it all went to shit.

364
00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:52.080
I fucked up.

365
00:22:58.680 --> 00:23:02.240
So. why is David the one being fired
if you shot the guy?

366
00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:05.120
He told Internal Investigations
it was him.

367
00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:06.640
Left me out.

368
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:09.440
He's doing it for me.

369
00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:12.320
And you're gonna let him?

370
00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:14.000
He's been lying from the start.

371
00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:18.400
Before he died. Mayard said that it's
David's fault that my dad was killed.

372
00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:21.280
How does that justify
what they're doing to him now?

373
00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:23.800
He needs to pay for what he's done.

374
00:23:25.080 --> 00:23:26.520
I agree. he does. of course.

375
00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:28.840
But not like this.

376
00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:41.120
[music fades]

377
00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:45.160
[motor revving]

378
00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:54.480
[motor shuts off]

379
00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.240
- I'm gonna tell them the truth.
- Don't do that.

380
00:24:13.320 --> 00:24:14.400
Look at me.

381
00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:17.360
Max. if you do this. you're done.

382
00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.000
My career's already over.

383
00:24:20.080 --> 00:24:21.480
- But that's…
- [door opens]

384
00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:23.560
[poignant music playing]

385
00:24:26.240 --> 00:24:29.440
My dad. Mayard said
it was your fault what happened to him.

386
00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:31.960
David. you're about
to destroy your life for me

387
00:24:32.040 --> 00:24:34.320
when a month ago.
you barely knew I existed.

388
00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:38.040
- Max…
- All I can think of is. you feel guilty.

389
00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:41.880
So unless you're ready to explain why
you're willing to sacrifice everything.

390
00:24:41.960 --> 00:24:43.080
I'm telling them the truth.

391
00:24:59.600 --> 00:25:03.320
[Christophe] The lone terrorist
used to work at the lab. He's an idealist.

392
00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:06.440
Angry about weapons they develop here.
he wants all of France to know.

393
00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:10.840
All they told me is that it's explosives.
Work in teams of two. usual partners.

394
00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:13.320
Standard rules of engagement.
reasonable self-defense.

395
00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:15.840
Imminent threat to a hostage's life.
or a direct order.

396
00:25:15.920 --> 00:25:17.800
Okay. everyone? Let's move!

397
00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:20.520
- [tense music playing]
- [man] Guys. let's move out.

398
00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:23.480
[indistinct chatter]

399
00:25:29.720 --> 00:25:32.360
Christophe. I wanna change partners.

400
00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:34.440
Change partners? Why?

401
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:36.920
It's better this way.

402
00:25:39.360 --> 00:25:40.600
Right. listen up. you two.

403
00:25:40.680 --> 00:25:42.840
I don't care what your problem is.
just handle it.

404
00:25:42.920 --> 00:25:45.120
There's a terrorist.
and 21 hostages that need us.

405
00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:47.200
You either make me regret
putting you in the field.

406
00:25:47.280 --> 00:25:49.160
or you figure your shit out.

407
00:25:51.120 --> 00:25:51.960
Okay.

408
00:25:53.960 --> 00:25:55.840
[suspenseful music playing]

409
00:25:56.720 --> 00:25:57.560
[door unlocks]

410
00:26:01.480 --> 00:26:04.120
- My daughter.
- [operator] Go! Go! Let's move it!

411
00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:05.480
Doc! Let's go!

412
00:26:05.560 --> 00:26:07.240
Listen. I'm a father too. okay?

413
00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:10.400
- I'm a father. I'll get your daughter.
- [fading] The lab…

414
00:26:10.480 --> 00:26:12.520
- We're getting out of here. now!
- [David] No. wait!

415
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.680
This way. come on! Here!

416
00:26:23.920 --> 00:26:25.440
We gotta be out in 50 seconds.

417
00:26:25.520 --> 00:26:27.800
- Lina!
- [David] Lina?

418
00:26:28.280 --> 00:26:29.120
- Lina!
- Lina!

419
00:26:29.200 --> 00:26:30.880
[Christophe on comm]
<i>Everyone. to the exits!</i>

420
00:26:30.960 --> 00:26:34.520
- [David] Lina. we're with your parents!
- Turn around. Get your asses outta there!

421
00:26:34.600 --> 00:26:35.600
<i>- You copy?</i>
- [David] Lina!

422
00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:37.720
- [Christophe] <i>Emergency procedure.</i>
- [David] Lina!

423
00:26:37.800 --> 00:26:39.880
- [Christophe] <i>Get out. right now!</i>
<i>- </i>Lina!

424
00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:42.200
Lina. if you're hiding in here.
you have to come out!

425
00:26:42.920 --> 00:26:43.760
David.

426
00:26:43.840 --> 00:26:46.080
<i>- I can't wait any longer. I'm doing it.</i>
- [Laurent] Lina!

427
00:26:46.160 --> 00:26:47.520
- [David] Lina!
- [sighs]

428
00:26:47.600 --> 00:26:50.200
- [alarm blaring]
- Laurent. we gotta move. Ah. fuck.

429
00:26:50.280 --> 00:26:52.040
- [Laurent] Lina!
- Laurent. let's go! Shit!

430
00:26:52.120 --> 00:26:54.320
- [Christophe] <i>David. that's an order! Out!</i>
<i>- </i>We have to go!

431
00:26:54.400 --> 00:26:56.240
Not until we've found her. Lina!

432
00:26:56.320 --> 00:26:57.840
- We have to fucking go. now!
- Lina!

433
00:26:57.920 --> 00:26:59.600
- Come on. move it!
- Let go!

434
00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:01.160
Let go of me!

435
00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:03.880
- [grunts]
- Get your hands off me! Don't touch me.

436
00:27:03.960 --> 00:27:05.120
Wait. Laurent.

437
00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:07.520
You know she's not here.
It's gonna blow. we've gotta leave.

438
00:27:07.600 --> 00:27:10.640
- So. then leave! You can fucking go!
- [gasps]

439
00:27:11.320 --> 00:27:14.040
[alarm blaring]

440
00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:17.040
[door whirring]

441
00:27:19.400 --> 00:27:21.080
[door locks]

442
00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:26.440
[dramatic music playing]

443
00:27:29.880 --> 00:27:31.880
[David grunting]

444
00:27:35.080 --> 00:27:36.120
[Laurent] David.

445
00:27:36.200 --> 00:27:37.280
Look at me!

446
00:27:38.720 --> 00:27:40.560
[pants] Just go. David.

447
00:27:41.360 --> 00:27:43.680
- There's gotta be another way outta here.
- There isn't.

448
00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:46.800
We both know it. Just go. please.

449
00:27:48.360 --> 00:27:49.400
Please.

450
00:27:55.680 --> 00:27:57.360
I'm sorry. Laurent.

451
00:27:57.960 --> 00:27:59.680
I'm so sorry.

452
00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:02.960
[David sobbing]

453
00:28:03.800 --> 00:28:05.080
[breathes shakily]

454
00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:06.440
Take care of Max.

455
00:28:07.560 --> 00:28:08.600
Okay.

456
00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:10.920
Get outta here.

457
00:28:12.960 --> 00:28:14.600
I said run!

458
00:28:15.520 --> 00:28:17.800
[dramatic music continues]

459
00:28:32.000 --> 00:28:33.640
[tools crashing]

460
00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:41.320
[exhales]

461
00:28:41.400 --> 00:28:43.160
[Laurent] I knew you were here.

462
00:28:46.960 --> 00:28:48.120
I'm Laurent.

463
00:28:49.320 --> 00:28:50.480
Come with me?

464
00:28:52.640 --> 00:28:55.080
[alarm blaring]

465
00:29:01.160 --> 00:29:02.640
It'll be okay.

466
00:29:03.600 --> 00:29:05.480
Is Mommy going to come and get me?

467
00:29:05.560 --> 00:29:06.960
[Laurent] Yeah. she's almost here.

468
00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:13.200
[muffled explosion]

469
00:29:14.920 --> 00:29:16.920
[music fades]

470
00:29:25.680 --> 00:29:27.680
There's something I don't understand.

471
00:29:29.280 --> 00:29:32.720
If none of this was your fault.
then why do this for me?

472
00:29:36.560 --> 00:29:38.520
Because it's still partially my fault.

473
00:29:40.080 --> 00:29:43.400
I mean that. uh… if Laurent's emotions
got the better of him.

474
00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:45.240
I played a part in that.

475
00:29:46.360 --> 00:29:48.680
[poignant music playing]

476
00:29:48.760 --> 00:29:50.640
He'd just received some results.

477
00:29:54.480 --> 00:29:56.760
He found out he couldn't have children.

478
00:29:58.160 --> 00:30:00.280
That he'd never been able to.

479
00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:07.600
{\an8}I'd held on to the secret for years.
at your mother's request but…

480
00:30:09.480 --> 00:30:11.160
I couldn't do it anymore.

481
00:30:13.560 --> 00:30:14.800
Max. I'm your dad.

482
00:30:23.640 --> 00:30:28.520
I know that… I know that I haven't really
been there for you since Laurent died.

483
00:30:28.600 --> 00:30:31.400
Your mother wanted me to keep my distance.
so I listened to her.

484
00:30:31.480 --> 00:30:34.200
Maybe I was an idiot for staying away.
I don't know.

485
00:30:34.280 --> 00:30:36.320
[poignant music continues]

486
00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:40.080
I-I-I just know I can't go back.
I can't change what happened.

487
00:30:41.720 --> 00:30:43.640
But I can make a difference now.

488
00:30:45.360 --> 00:30:46.240
For you.

489
00:30:50.840 --> 00:30:52.160
I can protect you.

490
00:30:55.960 --> 00:30:58.680
[Mélanie] We weren't expecting you
this morning. Major Villiers.

491
00:30:58.760 --> 00:31:01.040
[footsteps approach]

492
00:31:09.040 --> 00:31:10.000
Can we talk?

493
00:31:10.840 --> 00:31:11.760
Of course.

494
00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:15.800
[door opens]

495
00:31:28.080 --> 00:31:30.080
[poignant music continues]

496
00:31:36.440 --> 00:31:37.840
[exhales]

497
00:31:38.840 --> 00:31:40.600
I'll tell you what really happened.

498
00:31:41.960 --> 00:31:44.160
[music fades]

499
00:31:44.240 --> 00:31:45.520
[door opens]

500
00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:56.400
We'll be with you in five.

501
00:32:15.040 --> 00:32:16.440
[line dialing]

502
00:32:16.520 --> 00:32:19.080
[somber music playing]

503
00:32:21.200 --> 00:32:23.080
[breathing shakily]

504
00:32:23.160 --> 00:32:24.880
Hello. sweetheart. how's your day?

505
00:32:24.960 --> 00:32:26.440
You lied to me.

506
00:32:27.040 --> 00:32:28.280
What are you talking about?

507
00:32:28.840 --> 00:32:30.240
[sniffles]

508
00:32:30.320 --> 00:32:31.680
You lied about Dad and David.

509
00:32:32.720 --> 00:32:34.440
<i>How could you do that to me?</i>

510
00:32:35.120 --> 00:32:36.840
[Nathalie] <i>Hang on. Uh…</i>

511
00:32:36.920 --> 00:32:39.240
<i>- Where are you? We'll talk. okay?</i>
- [sobs]

512
00:32:39.320 --> 00:32:40.800
No. [exhales]

513
00:32:40.880 --> 00:32:42.160
<i>Tell me where you are.</i>

514
00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:44.040
- [sobs]
<i>- Max.</i>

515
00:32:45.880 --> 00:32:47.880
Max. just tell me so I can get there.

516
00:32:47.960 --> 00:32:49.960
- [sobs]
<i>- Please. Max.</i>

517
00:32:51.040 --> 00:32:52.640
[officer] Gentlemen. you ready?

518
00:32:55.960 --> 00:32:57.040
[sobs]

519
00:32:58.680 --> 00:33:00.680
- [line beeps]
- Damn it.

520
00:33:02.520 --> 00:33:06.160
[Mélanie] Rarely have I seen so many
violations of the GIGN's code of ethics.

521
00:33:06.240 --> 00:33:07.520
not to mention the law.

522
00:33:07.600 --> 00:33:10.680
You pursued the suspect on your own.
and got him killed.

523
00:33:10.760 --> 00:33:13.360
You acted in self-defense.
but the damage is still done.

524
00:33:13.440 --> 00:33:15.320
If it were up to me.
you'd be tried. convicted.

525
00:33:15.400 --> 00:33:17.880
A suspended sentence at the very least.

526
00:33:17.960 --> 00:33:20.200
And probably prison.
if we're being honest.

527
00:33:20.280 --> 00:33:22.720
But I don't think it would be beneficial.

528
00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:25.280
Not for the GIGN. nor the military police.

529
00:33:25.360 --> 00:33:26.880
if the two heroes of the hour.

530
00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:29.280
who put an end
to a bomber's murderous rampage.

531
00:33:29.360 --> 00:33:31.200
were publicly disciplined.

532
00:33:31.960 --> 00:33:33.040
Am I right. General?

533
00:33:33.120 --> 00:33:34.120
Yes.

534
00:33:34.200 --> 00:33:37.040
The fact remains that your actions
have no place in the armed forces.

535
00:33:37.120 --> 00:33:38.360
and even less in the GIGN.

536
00:33:38.440 --> 00:33:41.280
Commander. I expected more from you.

537
00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:44.480
You took a new recruit
on a clandestine operation.

538
00:33:44.560 --> 00:33:46.840
You are hereby suspended
pending early retirement.

539
00:33:46.920 --> 00:33:49.000
We never want to see you again.

540
00:33:49.080 --> 00:33:52.600
And you. Villiers. your inexperience
doesn't justify such a lapse of judgment.

541
00:33:52.680 --> 00:33:55.320
The disciplinary board
will decide your fate in two weeks.

542
00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:57.400
Until then.
you are prohibited from participating

543
00:33:57.480 --> 00:33:58.760
in any operations or training

544
00:33:58.840 --> 00:34:01.000
without the agreement
of your new section leader.

545
00:34:01.080 --> 00:34:04.280
I remind you that we have not yet found
the 500 kilos of explosives.

546
00:34:04.360 --> 00:34:07.320
I don't know what the final decision
will be regarding you. but let me say.

547
00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:10.080
this kind of crap has no place at GIGN.

548
00:34:11.080 --> 00:34:12.200
You're both dismissed.

549
00:34:12.280 --> 00:34:14.400
[music fades]

550
00:34:17.040 --> 00:34:18.600
[door opens]

551
00:34:20.680 --> 00:34:22.680
[poignant music playing]

552
00:34:25.080 --> 00:34:26.040
[David] Max!

553
00:34:31.120 --> 00:34:32.800
What else you wanna tell me?

554
00:34:34.240 --> 00:34:36.680
I gave everything to join the force.
Everything!

555
00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:40.280
All I wanted was to be like you and Dad!

556
00:34:41.560 --> 00:34:45.040
But what does it even matter?
You're not heroes! It's all bullshit!

557
00:34:46.040 --> 00:34:48.360
[poignant music continues]

558
00:34:50.480 --> 00:34:51.320
[engine starts]

559
00:34:57.000 --> 00:35:00.000
[tense music playing]

560
00:35:22.240 --> 00:35:23.880
[sighs]

561
00:35:24.520 --> 00:35:26.240
[man] It's not my fault!

562
00:35:26.840 --> 00:35:28.360
Fuck! What do we do?

563
00:35:29.560 --> 00:35:31.840
Just think. damn it! Think! Shit!

564
00:35:33.560 --> 00:35:35.880
[woman crying]

565
00:35:35.960 --> 00:35:37.960
[suspenseful music playing]

566
00:35:42.920 --> 00:35:43.800
[man] Shh!

567
00:35:47.520 --> 00:35:49.240
I've gone too far now.

568
00:35:49.320 --> 00:35:51.360
I'm not going back. Fuck.

569
00:35:52.040 --> 00:35:54.520
It's not my fault. It's not my fault.

570
00:35:55.720 --> 00:35:59.320
Sweetheart. you know
where Daddy's office is?

571
00:35:59.920 --> 00:36:03.560
Get yourself there.
Find a place to hide. Don't make a sound.

572
00:36:03.640 --> 00:36:06.120
Don't come out unless I'm telling you
it's safe to come out.

573
00:36:06.720 --> 00:36:07.800
Understand?

574
00:36:07.880 --> 00:36:09.960
I'll find you when it's safe. I promise.

575
00:36:10.560 --> 00:36:11.680
And you?

576
00:36:13.200 --> 00:36:15.040
[Amal] Don't worry. you know us.

577
00:36:15.120 --> 00:36:18.040
You know we're strong. you know
we won't stop fighting until we win.

578
00:36:18.120 --> 00:36:20.720
Get ready to move.
On my signal. you're gonna run.

579
00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:22.360
I'll come get you.

580
00:36:32.120 --> 00:36:34.000
- Go on. sweetheart.
- Run.

581
00:36:35.840 --> 00:36:37.720
- It's okay.
- Run. go on!

582
00:36:42.960 --> 00:36:44.960
[tense music playing]

583
00:36:52.000 --> 00:36:53.960
Calm down. Calm down.

584
00:36:54.560 --> 00:36:55.760
Calm down!

585
00:36:58.360 --> 00:36:59.400
[beeps]

586
00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:06.600
[man] You! Get up!

587
00:37:07.400 --> 00:37:08.920
Get the fuck up! Come on!

588
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:10.040
You too!

589
00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:11.440
On your feet!

590
00:37:12.200 --> 00:37:13.320
- Shit!
- [gunshots]

591
00:37:13.400 --> 00:37:14.360
[both groan]

592
00:37:16.600 --> 00:37:17.880
[screams]

593
00:37:17.960 --> 00:37:20.320
[intense music playing]

594
00:37:20.400 --> 00:37:22.280
Just stay with me. Stay with me.

595
00:37:23.200 --> 00:37:24.160
[beeps]

596
00:37:25.920 --> 00:37:27.320
- [man 1] Police!
- [man 2] Go! Go!

597
00:37:27.400 --> 00:37:29.360
[man 3] He planted explosives.

598
00:37:29.440 --> 00:37:31.040
- My daughter's in the lab!
- Get out.

599
00:37:31.120 --> 00:37:32.400
I'm a father too. okay?

600
00:37:32.480 --> 00:37:34.640
{\an8}I'm a father too.
I'm going to get your daughter.

601
00:37:34.720 --> 00:37:37.120
{\an8}[Amal] <i>I'll find you</i>
<i>when it's safe. I promise.</i>

602
00:37:37.200 --> 00:37:39.200
[intense music continues]

603
00:37:40.200 --> 00:37:42.760
- [metal rattling]
- [music fades]

604
00:37:52.000 --> 00:37:55.000
[metal shutter closes]

605
00:37:55.080 --> 00:37:57.680
[ominous music playing]

606
00:38:19.080 --> 00:38:21.080
[music turns suspenseful]

607
00:38:29.560 --> 00:38:31.520
A HUMAN TRAGEDY IN THE FACE
OF NATIONAL SECURITY

608
00:38:31.600 --> 00:38:33.640
LINA MAYARD 9 YEARS OLD
A LIFE CUT SHORT

609
00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:36.320
[music turns dramatic]

610
00:38:40.200 --> 00:38:42.760
[dramatic music continues]

611
00:39:14.880 --> 00:39:15.920
[music fades]

612
00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:19.280
Okay. you can sleep over at Nina's
but only if you promise you'll rehearse.

613
00:39:19.360 --> 00:39:20.680
- [Manon] <i>Okay.</i>
- Don't go anywhere.

614
00:39:20.760 --> 00:39:23.360
Don't worry. we're going to school first
to practice for a bit.

615
00:39:23.440 --> 00:39:24.680
Then we'll go to Nina's.

616
00:39:24.760 --> 00:39:26.680
<i>- Night. Mom. Love you.</i>
<i>- </i>I love you too. sweetie.

617
00:39:26.760 --> 00:39:29.720
- [elevator chimes]
- [doors open]

618
00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:34.520
[poignant music playing]

619
00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:43.360
I've been suspended.

620
00:39:43.440 --> 00:39:44.400
What?

621
00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:47.280
I told Max everything.

622
00:39:49.080 --> 00:39:50.800
I told him he's my son.

623
00:39:54.480 --> 00:39:58.000
And then. that idiot decided
to tell the inspector the truth.

624
00:39:58.080 --> 00:40:00.360
even though he was in the clear.

625
00:40:01.160 --> 00:40:02.320
[sighs]

626
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:05.920
You were going to end up in prison
so that Max could stay on the force? How…?

627
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:08.720
- What kind of a plan was that?
- [sighs]

628
00:40:08.800 --> 00:40:11.000
Jess. you know
I made a promise to Laurent.

629
00:40:11.080 --> 00:40:14.160
I swore to him I would take care of Max.

630
00:40:14.240 --> 00:40:16.600
I promised him I'd take care of Max.

631
00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:18.160
I promised him.

632
00:40:18.240 --> 00:40:23.120
COMMIT FOR LIFE
NATIONAL MILITARY POLICE

633
00:40:26.760 --> 00:40:29.480
- [inaudible dialogue]
- [poignant music continues]

634
00:40:31.960 --> 00:40:34.360
[Jess] <i>And you really think</i>
<i>that's why you're doing all this?</i>

635
00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:37.120
That's bullshit.

636
00:40:37.200 --> 00:40:40.400
If you hadn't made that promise.
you'd still be acting this way.

637
00:40:41.200 --> 00:40:43.920
The truth is you feel guilty
about what happened.

638
00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:46.840
You can't get rid of that feeling
no matter how hard you try.

639
00:40:48.920 --> 00:40:51.080
Who's going to give you permission
to start living?

640
00:40:51.560 --> 00:40:54.480
When will you let yourself
be with your family?

641
00:40:54.560 --> 00:40:56.480
<i>You're not guilty of anything.</i>

642
00:40:56.560 --> 00:40:57.800
[David] <i>I am. though.</i>

643
00:41:00.200 --> 00:41:02.600
Because I did. I did betray Laurent.

644
00:41:04.360 --> 00:41:07.280
I shouldn't have said what I said to him
right before the mission…

645
00:41:07.360 --> 00:41:09.640
[sobbing]

646
00:41:09.720 --> 00:41:12.200
And I'm guilty of not looking out for Max.

647
00:41:12.960 --> 00:41:16.160
- [David sobbing]
- [poignant music continues]

648
00:41:17.440 --> 00:41:19.800
I wasn't there for him.
for my son. for fuck's sake.

649
00:41:19.880 --> 00:41:21.440
I wasn't there for my kid.

650
00:41:25.520 --> 00:41:26.440
[David sobs]

651
00:41:28.200 --> 00:41:31.360
And I've never been there for you either.
not really. I haven't.

652
00:41:31.440 --> 00:41:33.320
[sobbing]

653
00:41:33.400 --> 00:41:35.280
I'm there for everyone.
except for my family.

654
00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:36.800
You needed me and I wasn't there.

655
00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:38.880
[poignant music intensifies]

656
00:41:52.200 --> 00:41:54.720
[screams]

657
00:42:03.400 --> 00:42:04.760
[sniffles]

658
00:42:04.840 --> 00:42:05.960
I'm sorry.

659
00:42:08.360 --> 00:42:09.440
I'm so sorry.

660
00:42:09.520 --> 00:42:11.560
[screams]

661
00:42:13.520 --> 00:42:15.520
[music fades]

662
00:42:17.120 --> 00:42:20.200
[playing "Nocturne No. 13"
by Frédéric Chopin]

663
00:43:02.520 --> 00:43:04.680
- [weapons cocking]
- [piano stops]

664
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:08.280
[menacing music playing]

665
00:43:19.240 --> 00:43:20.520
I'm so sorry.

666
00:43:26.720 --> 00:43:28.280
[music fades]

667
00:43:29.120 --> 00:43:31.600
[dramatic music playing]

668
00:48:52.240 --> 00:48:53.320
[music ends]

669
00:48:54.305 --> 00:49:54.629
